Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.789 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  reese witherspoon opens up about facing  psychological and verbal abuse in a past  relationship during an interview with  her wrinkle and time co-star Oprah  Winfrey as part of super soul Sunday the  41 year old actress gets candid about  the quote most difficult decision she  ever had to make  leaving an abusive relationship a line  got drawn in the sand and it got crossed  and my brain just switched and I knew it  was gonna be very difficult but I just  couldn't go any further  Witherspoon explains that it was this  moment that altered the trajectory of  her life I couldn't ever be the person I  am today I was a different person - it  changed who I was on a cellular level  the fact that I stopped for myself I'm a  different person now and it's part of  the reason I can stand up and say yes  I'm ambitious and yes because someone  tried to take that from me et caught up  with the actress at the Golden Globes in  January where she talked about the times  up movement aimed in part at fighting  abuse people who were so brave to tell  their stories first and we're standing  here because of the courage they had and  also women in all industries and men in  all industries are standing up and  saying enough with discrimination and  harassment and abuse we deserve equality  and the time is up  [Music]

